# checks that flag handling is case insensitive, as it should be.
#
# depends on obliterate to remove both lowercase, LOWERCASE abd
# LoWeRCaSe from flag_names before the store.
#
depends append
send 1
a fetch 1 flags
receive 2
* 1 FETCH (FLAGS (\Recent))
a OK done
send 1
b store 1 +flags lowercase LOWERCASE LoWeRCaSe
receive 4
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen lowercase)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen lowercase \*)] permanent flags
* 1 FETCH (UID 1 FLAGS (\Recent lowercase))
b OK done
send 3
c store 1 +flags lowercase
c store 1 +flags lowercase
c store 1 +flags lowercase
receive 3
c OK done
c OK done
c OK done
# The first store of a new flag goes alone. Three at once would race to
# create it, two could both write, and the number of FETCH responses
# would depend on the timing.
send 1
d store 1 +flags UPPERCASE
receive 4
* FLAGS (UPPERCASE \Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen lowercase)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (UPPERCASE \Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen lowercase \*)] permanent flags
* 1 FETCH (UID 1 FLAGS (\Recent lowercase UPPERCASE))
d OK done
send 2
d store 1 +flags UPPERCASE
d store 1 +flags UPPERCASE
receive 2
d OK done
d OK done
send 3
e store 1 +flags Uppercase
e store 1 +flags UPpercase
e store 1 +flags UPPercase
receive 3
e OK done
e OK done
e OK done
end
